window.bookSummaryJSON = "<b>From the <i>New York Times</i> bestselling author of <i>Before I Let Go </i>comes a powerful forbidden romance about one woman on the brink of making a life-altering decision.</b><br><br> Kerris Moreton knows how to make things work. Bounced from foster home to foster home as a kid, she adapted; when opportunity arose, she thrived. Now, about to open her own business and accept a marriage proposal, Kerris is ready to build the life she's always wanted.<br><br> The only thing missing? A passionate connection with her would-be fiance, Cam. Kerris wants to believe that sparks are overrated—until Walsh Bennett lights her up like the Fourth of July.<br><br> As one of the East Coast's most eligible bachelors, Walsh enjoys financial independence, fulfilling work with his family's nonprofit, and plenty of female attention. But lately he's been distracted by the one woman he can't have.<br><br> Lovely to look at and even sweeter to know, Kerris is the soulmate Walsh never thought he would find. The problem is, his best friend found her first."; 
